  "_comment": "A task the owl sets aloud. `accepted` is matched against what on-device recognition heard, loosely — see QuestionMatcher. `reveal` is what the owl says when the answer was not on the list: it offers an answer of its own and moves on. There is no wrong, no score and no streak.",
  "_fallback": "`choices` exists for the no-recognition path: when SFSpeechRecognizer is unavailable the child taps one of these pictures instead of speaking. The first entry is the correct one and the mode shuffles them. They are picture names, not spoken answers — tapping the cow answers 'what sound does a cow make', so `choices` and `accepted` deliberately differ.",
